   - Architecture: Client-Side Single Page Application (SPA)
   - Live URL: https://aura-finance-silk.vercel.app/

2. SUMMARY OF MANDATORY DELIVERABLES:
   - Problem Definition: Detailed in Section 2 of Project Report.
   - Design Specifications: Full responsive design system detailed in Section 5.
   - Flowcharts & DFDs: Complete Mermaid diagrams included in Section 8.
   - Test Data: Structured JSON test files located in /public/test-data/.
   - Installation Manual: Step-by-step commands detailed in Section 12.
   - Video Walkthrough Script: Structured 5-minute video guide in docs/DEMO_VIDEO_SCRIPT.md.

3. ARCHITECTURAL ASSUMPTIONS MADE AT OUR END (SRS Section 1.9):
   a. Client-Side Privacy:
      Per SRS Section 1.2 & 1.5, the application operates with 100% client-side
      persistence. No remote relational backend (e.g. MySQL/MongoDB) or server-side
      database is utilized. State persistence is managed through IndexedDB (Dexie.js)
      and Web Storage, ensuring zero user data leakage and immediate offline capability.

   b. Currency Support:
      While standard test currency defaults to USD ($), multi-currency toggle support
      (PKR ₨, EUR €, GBP £) has been built into the top navigation bar to facilitate
      international student evaluation without altering underlying ratio algorithms.

   c. Persona Simulation:
      To accelerate evaluators' assessment of the platform, a 1-click Quick-Start
      Persona selector (College Student, Tech Freelancer, Family Household, Clean Slate)
      has been integrated to instantly seed realistic data into all calculators.

   d. Educational Scope:
      BudgetBasics is designed as an educational and behavioral awareness platform.
      All calculators present mathematical simulations and estimates for learning
      purposes only, without claiming banking, custodial, or investment services.

   e. Extended Commerce Simulator:
      For accounting students requiring advanced double-entry practice beyond basic
      cash budgeting, an optional General Ledger simulator has been included in the
      "More" menu with atomic debit-credit balance validation ($Dr = $Cr).

4. SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS & RUNTIME:
   - Node.js: Version 18.0.0 or higher
   - Package Manager: npm (v9+) or pnpm
   - Recommended Browser: Google Chrome 120+, Mozilla Firefox 120+, Microsoft Edge 120+
   - Display: Responsive layout optimized for 375px (Mobile) to 1920px (Desktop)

5. QUICK START INSTALLATION:
   Step 1: Extract project archive into workspace directory.
   Step 2: Open terminal in project root.
   Step 3: Run 'npm install' to install dependencies.
   Step 4: Run 'npm run dev' to launch local development server (http://localhost:5173).
   Step 5: Run 'npm run build' to compile production bundle (zero warnings/errors).

6. TEST DATA LOCATIONS:
   - /public/test-data/sample_student_budget.json
   - /public/test-data/sample_spending_categories.json
   - /public/test-data/sample_savings_goals.json
   - /public/test-data/test_data_readme.txt

7. AI USAGE ACKNOWLEDGEMENT:
   In compliance with SRS Page 12 ("Important Note Regarding AI Usage"), AI-assisted
   tools (Google Antigravity, Figma AI, Canva AI) were utilized as productivity aids
   for brainstorming, code validation, and icon generation. All architectural design,
   state management, component implementation, and responsive styling were manually
   engineered, debugged, and verified by the development team.

